Research spike #5, MFO-natural reframing of §XIII.1.

KEY REFRAMING (per user): MFO's "field-fundamental, spatial emerges"
ontology makes log(m²/m_ref²) the natural mass variable, not m. Linear-mass
search (spikes 1-4) was a category error — assumed visual/spatial primacy
that MFO ontology rejects.

In log-m² space, SM charged fermions live in bounded [0, 25.5]:
  e=0, u=2.88, d=4.43, s=10.42, μ=10.66, c=15.64, τ=16.31, b=18.02, t=25.46

This eliminates the "massive span" problem (11 orders of magnitude in
linear mass² → bounded 25.5 in log space). Fractal eigenvalue spectra
can naturally fit in this range.

STRUCTURAL FEATURES TESTED:
  - 3-cluster pattern (light/middle/heavy)
  - Near-degeneracies: (s,μ) gap 0.25, (c,τ) gap 0.67
  - Total span ~25.5

  RESULT: null test shows 25.3% of random 9-value scatters in [0, 25.5]
  reproduce this signature. Structural features as defined are NOT
  strong enough to be signal — they happen often by chance.

CANDIDATE FITS (linear regression of candidate eigenvalues to SM log-m²):
  SG3_first9     R² = 0.9503  max_resid = 3.79  (44× off in mass²)
  SG2 × CP²      R² = 0.9187  max_resid = 3.42
  SG3 × S²       R² = 0.8754  max_resid = 4.91
  Round spheres  R² ≈ 0.75
  None achieves residuals small enough to be a real physics fit.

VERDICT: MFO-natural reframing fixes the structural framing
(bounded problem, log-space, field-primary) but does not by itself
identify THE candidate. Eigenvalue matching alone — even in the right
variable — is too information-poor.

CRITICAL OBSERVATION: I truncated to 9 charged fermions, but SM has 12
fermions including 3 neutrinos at ln(m_ν²/m_e²) ≈ −27.6. Total fermion
span is −27.6 to +25.5, roughly SYMMETRIC around 0 (the electron). A
log-symmetric spectrum is exactly what chiral-fermion mechanisms predict
and a much stronger structural feature than what we tested. Next spike
should include neutrinos and test for log-symmetric structure.

CUMULATIVE STATE (5 spikes):
  #1 Forward eigenvalue search   → no fit
  #2 SG-decimation inverse        → refuted
  #3 Universal-b sweep            → Diophantine-degenerate
  #4 Multiplicity test            → tautological
  #5 MFO log-mass space           → bounded but no clean fit

If spike #6 (full 12-fermion log-symmetric test) also fails, the
honest endpoint is: §XIII.1 as currently articulated cannot be
verified by eigenvalue-based methods, and audit of its provenance
(including potential Gemini-CLI taint per [[project_may8_commit_gemini_taint_caveat]])
is the warranted next move.

